    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Here is what I have for 48 prostate tumors: an expression table with genes in rows and samples in columns, a regulator-gene-weight motif edge list, a TF-TF interaction edge list, and a README describing how the samples were collected. I want to know how active each TF is in each tumor and whether each TF activates or represses its targets."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"how active each TF is in each tumor\" -- available from GIRAFFE.\n2. \"whether each TF activates or represses its targets\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n\n**GIRAFFE**. GIRAFFE jointly factors expression into a regulatory-effect matrix and sample-varying TF activities using biological priors. Signed effects describe the fitted activation/repression relationship, while activity differs from the TF's own expression. These fitted coefficients do not alone establish causality.\n\nYou would need expression matrix, motif/prior, PPI network. The analysis would provide inferred regulator-to-target associations; inferred transcription-factor-by-sample activity values.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
